warning[LINT017]: `cond` on `<transition>` is an arrow function, so it is always true
 --> tests/ui/lint017-ecmascript-arrow-condition.scx:7:42
  |
7 |     <transition event="go4" cond="(a, b) => a" target="b"/>
  |                                          ^^ `=>` makes an arrow function
  |
  = note: in ECMAScript `x => 1` is a function whose parameter is `x`; a condition is converted to a boolean without calling it, and every function is truthy, so the condition always holds
  = help: a condition must compute a boolean: compare with `>=`, or call the function
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model

